python-validity (0.16~hp18) noble; urgency=medium

  * Allow the captured d51 clean-slate sequence for the second independently
    reproduced zero-partition identity: 06cb:00b7 / 0xd51 / FM-3439-001.
    Keep every other 00b7 variant fail-closed; that USB ID also contains 0x969
    devices whose reset/format sequence remains unproven.
  * Add regression coverage preventing inferred clean-slate writes to related
    but unvalidated sensor variants.
  * Log successful and wrong-template match outcomes at INFO level so
    long-duration stability tests can distinguish real matches from silent
    client cancellation without exposing biometric or template material.
  * Keep package installation hardware-safe: cache firmware and reload rules,
    but do not globally retrigger udev, start the daemon inside dpkg, or modify
    PAM automatically. Matched hardware starts through udev on the next real
    add event (normally the next boot).
  * Restrict the startup USB-reset recovery to 138a:00ab and 06cb:00b7, the
    exact device families with observed first-command wedges. Legacy readers
    and 06cb:00cb retain their established startup behavior.
  * Replace stale d51/969 reset guidance with the validated per-device
    provisioned/clean-slate support matrix.
  * Deepen the 138a:00ab clean-slate guard from VID:PID-only to the complete
    captured ROM and sensor identity. The same USB ID exists with 0x969
    hardware, so it must never inherit the d51 write sequence by inference.
  * Recover only the documented interrupted-fwext state: if partition 2
    returns signature error 044f, erase that incomplete firmware partition and
    re-upload it. Leave every other firmware probe error non-destructive.

